WEBVTT

00:06.737 --> 00:09.697
This must be the moment 
I've been waiting for.

00:10.477 --> 00:12.827
What could we possibly
 hope to accomplish?

00:13.567 --> 00:15.207
I have knowledge.

00:15.857 --> 00:19.167
Let me serve you 
as your new jada stone, Highness.

00:19.557 --> 00:21.967
Please lend me your power.

00:24.187 --> 00:27.387
Let the two of us summon a storm.

00:36.007 --> 00:37.847
<i>What have I done?</i>

00:37.847 --> 00:40.507
<i>Not only did I ignore
Princess Sorghaghtani's orders...</i>

00:42.197 --> 00:44.877
<i>Wait, I'm...</i>

00:50.547 --> 00:53.287
<i>I'm not Sorghaghtani's slave.</i>

00:55.507 --> 00:57.097
Ah, there you are.

00:57.097 --> 00:58.417
Fatima!

00:58.737 --> 01:00.547
I've been looking for you!

00:59.187 --> 01:05.207
<i>Lady Töregene has bore her undulled pain
for longer than I have mine.</i>

01:00.547 --> 01:05.407
If you failed to get in, you should return
to Princess Sorghaghtani at once.

01:05.407 --> 01:07.257
Hey, Fatima.

01:05.937 --> 01:06.807
<i>Which is why...</i>

01:07.957 --> 01:10.217
Tell Princess Sorghaghtani this.

01:10.567 --> 01:13.847
I've found my way into 
a more <i>convenient</i> position.

01:14.107 --> 01:16.017
I-Is that right?

01:16.417 --> 01:18.207
All the better, then.

01:20.657 --> 01:23.607
<i>No need to worry. I understand now.</i>

01:24.327 --> 01:26.027
<i>I know what I must do.</i>

01:30.657 --> 01:34.237
<i>Just you wait, Mongols.</i>

01:49.907 --> 01:52.597
<b>Jaadugar</b>

03:12.277 --> 03:16.777
<b>Brothers</b>

03:26.577 --> 03:28.177
What's this now, Chagatai?

03:33.217 --> 03:35.247
I offer my deepest apologies.

03:37.447 --> 03:40.507
Not only did I challenge 
the Great Kha'an to a wager,

03:40.507 --> 03:43.537
I displayed the utmost 
insolence by winning.

03:43.537 --> 03:45.127
Oh, you mean that?

03:48.177 --> 03:53.207
For such a grave offense, I am prepared 
to face a flogging—nay, a death sentence.

03:53.207 --> 03:54.817
Please do with me as you will.

03:59.137 --> 04:03.107
With this, you are forgiven.
 You know I am not angered so easily.

04:07.517 --> 04:10.647
Ögedei Kha'an has shown me his mercy!

04:10.647 --> 04:13.147
Praise be his magnanimity!

04:13.487 --> 04:17.557
Huzzah! Huzzah!

04:17.557 --> 04:20.237
Huzzah!

04:17.857 --> 04:20.237
Huh? What?

04:23.257 --> 04:24.577
With this, I take my leave.

04:30.057 --> 04:32.417
I swear, what was the meaning of that?

04:32.417 --> 04:34.967
Prince Chagatai put on 
that performance for your sake.

04:35.107 --> 04:37.677
<b>Chief Scribe
Chinqai</b>

04:35.417 --> 04:36.537
Chinqai.

04:37.957 --> 04:40.577
It hasn't been long since you took 
the throne as Ögedei Kha'an.

04:40.577 --> 04:43.437
Honor upon your name 
is what you require most at this time.

04:43.437 --> 04:46.517
And what quality is prized 
among steppe tribe leaders?

04:46.857 --> 04:48.187
Magnanimity.

04:48.417 --> 04:49.627
Exactly.

04:49.627 --> 04:52.717
Merciless to his foes, 
yet magnanimous to his subjects.

04:52.717 --> 04:55.647
You've now shown yourself 
to be just that, Great Kha'an.

04:55.647 --> 04:59.427
I understand, but does he need
 to be so dramatic?

05:02.657 --> 05:03.787
Oh, I see now.

05:04.507 --> 05:06.027
Magnanimity, is it?

05:08.767 --> 05:14.467
<i>Kurultais were held under Ögedei Kha'an 
to discuss matters of future policy.</i>

05:15.277 --> 05:17.177
<i>What's more, in the Mongol Empire,</i>

05:17.177 --> 05:20.927
<i>the emperor's consorts took part
 in these political matters.</i>

05:24.187 --> 05:25.307
Töregene?

05:25.607 --> 05:29.457
What are <i>you</i> doing at a kurultai?
I hardly ever see you attend one.

05:29.457 --> 05:30.607
Am I not allowed?

05:30.887 --> 05:33.557
There are <i>some</i> who wish 
to attend, but cannot.

05:41.797 --> 05:46.537
<b>Temüge's Son
Otai</b>

05:41.797 --> 05:46.537
<b>Genghis Khan's
Younger Brother
Temüge</b>

05:42.097 --> 05:43.327
Listen to me, Uqai.

05:43.327 --> 05:46.547
I'm Otai. Please try to remember
 my name, Father.

05:47.377 --> 05:50.697
Today's discussion will outline
our next military campaign.

05:47.597 --> 06:15.607
<b>Jin Dynasty</b>

05:47.597 --> 06:15.607
<b>Southern Song</b>

05:50.697 --> 05:53.657
Our target is the Jin dynasty, 
our long-standing enemies to the east.

05:53.657 --> 05:58.477
I hear many of our forefathers 
were abducted and killed by the Jin.

05:58.477 --> 06:01.927
Yes, but truth be told, 
that's of little consequence now.

06:02.567 --> 06:05.047
The House of Tolui
has the largest military.

06:02.987 --> 06:13.087
<b>House of Tolui</b>

06:05.047 --> 06:07.907
The House of Chagatai, 
which the Great Kha'an has great trust in.

06:06.037 --> 06:13.087
<b>House of Chagatai</b>

06:07.037 --> 06:13.087
<b>House of Jochi</b>

06:07.907 --> 06:11.557
Jochi, the head of the House of Jochi, 
is dead, and his territory is far away.

06:10.287 --> 06:13.087
<b>House of Ögedei</b>

06:11.377 --> 06:15.607
<b>House of Temüge</b>

06:11.827 --> 06:15.607
And my own territory, that of 
the House of Temüge, is close to the Jin.

06:15.607 --> 06:19.277
Now that our houses rule over
 a great deal of subjects,

06:19.277 --> 06:22.487
we all want a role for ourselves 
that won't incur losses.

06:22.487 --> 06:26.847
How will the new Kha'an fare
 in appeasing us all?

06:26.847 --> 06:28.167
What say you, Daritai?

06:28.167 --> 06:29.267
It's Otai.

06:34.707 --> 06:39.497
How will you handle this, Great Kha'an?

06:45.837 --> 06:47.767
I wish to build a capital.

06:49.437 --> 06:50.687
<i>Uh-oh.</i>

06:53.537 --> 06:54.857
A capital?

06:54.857 --> 06:56.927
Yes, a capital.

06:56.927 --> 06:59.217
We will construct a city in the steppe.

06:59.217 --> 07:01.817
One of permanent buildings, not tents.

07:02.097 --> 07:04.357
Wh-What are you going on about?

07:04.357 --> 07:06.517
What of the Jin campaign?

07:06.517 --> 07:07.917
A capital, you say?

07:07.917 --> 07:09.787
Do we have to live there?

07:09.787 --> 07:13.537
Mongols take pride in crossing mountains
 in pursuit of unseen lands.

07:13.537 --> 07:16.437
Live like settled people? Disgusting.

07:16.437 --> 07:19.757
Everyone, the Great Kha'an 
hasn't finished speaking.

07:20.347 --> 07:23.447
It will be a capital, 
but not one for us to live in.

07:23.447 --> 07:26.737
It will provide workshops 
for crafting weapons and jewelry,

07:26.737 --> 07:30.887
and also serve as a trading post 
where foreign merchants can gather.

07:31.377 --> 07:34.117
We will continue our nomadic lifestyles.

07:34.117 --> 07:37.567
But at times, we will stop by the capital
 to spend extravagantly.

07:37.567 --> 07:39.897
In a show of our generosity 
and magnanimity.

07:39.897 --> 07:44.807
Word of it is sure to attract people 
and goods from across the land.

07:45.197 --> 07:46.047
What say you?

07:46.727 --> 07:48.657
I don't see the sense in it.

07:51.397 --> 07:52.767
Does my idea lack merit?

07:55.567 --> 07:57.157
Sounds great to me!

08:01.847 --> 08:04.677
A curious proposal, indeed. 
I think it's worth doing.

08:05.877 --> 08:06.927
Tolui.

08:07.317 --> 08:09.097
By the way, Great Kha'an...

08:13.257 --> 08:15.437
When will we broach the subject of war?

08:16.807 --> 08:18.487
What?

08:19.517 --> 08:23.737
At last, the time is ripe to do away 
with the Jin, our long sworn foes!

08:23.737 --> 08:28.707
<b>Mongols</b>

08:23.737 --> 08:29.137
<b>Jin Dynasty</b>

08:24.497 --> 08:26.707
Their formerly vast territory has shrunk.

08:26.707 --> 08:28.717
Now they're cornered like tiny rats.

08:28.717 --> 08:32.097
The one to deal the final blow
 will be our Great Kha'an!

08:33.597 --> 08:38.857
<b>Kaifeng</b>

08:34.117 --> 08:36.247
This war will be just like a circle hunt.

08:36.557 --> 08:39.277
The hunting ground will be 
the Jin capital, Kaifeng.

08:39.277 --> 08:44.087
The Great Kha'an will first set up camp 
 across the Yellow River, north of Kaifeng.

08:44.087 --> 08:48.007
While the rats tremble in fear, 
we will pincer them from the south.

08:48.377 --> 08:51.507
That sounds more like 
hunting deer than rats.

08:51.507 --> 08:53.727
Call them fawns if it makes you happy.

08:53.727 --> 08:56.337
Tolui, the Jin mustn't be underestimated.

08:56.337 --> 09:00.727
Even on the verge of collapse, they vastly
outnumber us in soldiers and subjects.

09:02.187 --> 09:06.357
Uncle, that's why I want you to send
 their citizens running from the east.

09:07.757 --> 09:10.547
Just like you would coax animals 
into a hunting circle,

09:10.547 --> 09:15.157
if we can chase the Jin populace
 inside Kaifeng's walls,

09:15.157 --> 09:19.957
all those soldiers and subjects 
will be trapped in a closed-off city.

09:20.697 --> 09:23.207
After winter passes
 and their food runs out,

09:23.207 --> 09:25.717
what state will the city be in?

09:29.947 --> 09:32.137
Oh, as for you, Brother Chagatai.

09:32.137 --> 09:35.097
I think it's best if you stay in Mongolia 
to look after affairs.

09:35.407 --> 09:39.987
We should leave our home to the one 
the Great Kha'an trusts most.

09:39.987 --> 09:40.707
Right?

09:41.857 --> 09:43.767
Well, that's fine by me.

09:46.827 --> 09:49.737
Jochi's kin won't have a part 
to play here, I'm afraid.

09:49.737 --> 09:51.267
What?

09:52.407 --> 09:56.867
In exchange, you'll be leading 
the campaigns to the west.

09:58.737 --> 09:59.997
How does that sound?

10:00.417 --> 10:02.957
Are any of you unhappy 
with these war plans?

10:05.797 --> 10:06.877
Prince Tolui.

10:07.917 --> 10:13.207
We must enter Southern Song territory
to approach Kaifeng from the south.

10:13.207 --> 10:15.847
Through precipitous 
mountain roads at that.

10:15.847 --> 10:19.707
That poses no problem. The Southern Song
 considers the Jin an enemy.

10:19.707 --> 10:21.667
The enemy of our enemy is our friend.

10:21.667 --> 10:24.267
As for the precipitous mountains...

10:25.217 --> 10:26.317
We'll persevere.

10:31.347 --> 10:34.077
That's everything I heard at the kurultai.

10:34.557 --> 10:36.497
Thank you very much.

10:37.387 --> 10:42.957
<i>If Tolui's plans succeed, starvation 
and cold await the people of Kaifeng.</i>

10:43.727 --> 10:46.487
<i>I'm confronted with 
this knowledge, and yet...</i>

10:47.377 --> 10:50.547
Do you feel unwell, Sitara? 
You're trembling.

10:52.167 --> 10:54.487
My apologies. I'm fine.

10:56.047 --> 10:57.187
Sitara.

11:00.597 --> 11:04.877
Lady Töregene. Please call me Fatima.

11:04.877 --> 11:06.147
Fatima?

11:06.147 --> 11:09.697
Sitara is my name from when I was a slave.

11:10.227 --> 11:14.777
It'd be improper for someone of low birth 
to serve the Great Kha'an's consort.

11:17.207 --> 11:19.937
I, too, pass myself off as a Naiman here.

11:21.537 --> 11:26.157
Having married a Merkit man, 
I would call myself a Merkit,

11:26.157 --> 11:29.127
but there are many Mongols 
who don't take kindly to them.

11:29.917 --> 11:35.057
That's why I chose to keep my past 
as a Merkit a secret from everyone.

11:37.667 --> 11:40.417
Please keep it a secret too, Fatima.

11:41.137 --> 11:41.897
I will.

11:42.917 --> 11:45.157
<i>She has the scent of danger about her.</i>

11:45.857 --> 11:48.567
So where do we go from here?

11:48.567 --> 11:53.317
There is indeed a power imbalance between 
the Great Kha'an and the Tolui family.

11:53.317 --> 11:56.527
The House of Tolui commands 
the largest Mongol army,

11:56.527 --> 11:58.287
the Great Kha'an 
has the highest authority,

11:58.727 --> 12:00.857
and the House of Chagatai supports him.

12:01.297 --> 12:03.527
We must cause a rift between them.

12:04.017 --> 12:05.537
In order to accomplish that,

12:05.757 --> 12:09.577
we need Prince Tolui's plans to succeed.

12:14.927 --> 12:16.427
Pardon the intrusion.

12:20.257 --> 12:22.287
How are you feeling, Boraqchin?

12:24.267 --> 12:27.297
Seeing your face has brightened
 my mood a little.

12:25.167 --> 12:28.017
<b>Great Khatun
Boraqchin</b>

12:28.017 --> 12:29.867
What's that?

12:29.867 --> 12:33.037
A medical text brought here
 by Quanzhen Daoists.

12:34.597 --> 12:38.547
Our bodies, in the process of living, 
gradually lose the qi they started with,

12:38.547 --> 12:40.577
eventually leading
to maladies and death.

12:40.577 --> 12:44.287
Through training, 
you can stop the flow of qi.

12:44.287 --> 12:48.337
That's their technique 
to achieve immortality, it seems.

12:50.047 --> 12:53.547
Will those techniques return you 
to health, Boraqchin?

12:54.017 --> 12:55.257
Möge.

12:55.907 --> 13:01.697
You're supposed to be the one sitting 
at the Great Kha'an's side for kurultais.

13:02.787 --> 13:05.267
You, the cleverest of us all.

13:07.727 --> 13:11.187
Political matters are not decided
 by kurultais alone.

13:12.477 --> 13:16.437
What is important is to discreetly 
maneuver all manner of affairs.

13:17.107 --> 13:18.217
Now, Möge.

13:18.627 --> 13:21.157
Tell me everything you heard.

13:23.957 --> 13:27.537
This plan entails Prince Tolui 
bearing a great burden,

13:27.537 --> 13:31.377
but in return, should he succeed, 
he will earn the most acclaim.

13:31.847 --> 13:34.337
And he will most likely succeed.

13:35.017 --> 13:39.247
The House of Tolui has the strongest army
 of the Mongols, after all.

13:39.637 --> 13:44.897
The Mongol army's audacious tactics 
are sure to startle the enemy.

13:45.807 --> 13:46.887
However...

13:47.357 --> 13:51.897
However, the other Mongol princes 
will reach the same conclusion.

13:52.217 --> 13:53.857
That the House of Tolui...

13:54.117 --> 13:55.317
...is too powerful.

13:54.117 --> 13:55.317
...is too powerful.

13:57.237 --> 14:00.207
Even if Tolui himself 
doesn't intend to betray anyone,

14:00.627 --> 14:04.867
should the other houses fear his strength 
and harbor distrust,

14:05.347 --> 14:10.527
and should they collude against 
the House of Tolui, I'm certain that...

14:12.617 --> 14:16.547
The Mongols will fracture, 
and eventually fall to ruin.

14:16.547 --> 14:20.357
There will be those who aim 
to sow the seeds of discord.

14:20.357 --> 14:22.297
So what can we do?

14:22.627 --> 14:26.567
Möge, you are young 
and attractive, unlike me.

14:26.567 --> 14:28.567
You are an honest and amiable girl.

14:30.057 --> 14:32.667
To ensure the Mongols are not divided,

14:32.667 --> 14:38.527
and to ensure our hearts remain as one, 
I need you to take steps in my stead.

14:40.657 --> 14:42.977
If you say so, Boraqchin.

14:46.737 --> 14:51.457
<i>Driven into a closed-off city 
to perish from hunger and cold...</i>

14:51.817 --> 14:54.457
<i>The people of Tus 
could have met the same fate.</i>

14:55.737 --> 15:01.087
<i>To the citizens of Kaifeng, 
I am just another Mongol.</i>

15:10.937 --> 15:14.917
<b>Summer, A.D. 1230</b>

15:10.937 --> 15:14.917
<b>Domain of the House of Ögedei</b>

15:18.937 --> 15:23.997
The Great Kha'an heads to war as 
Prince Chagatai stays to watch the steppe.

15:23.997 --> 15:25.907
What shall we be doing?

15:26.417 --> 15:29.747
We will accompany the Great Kha'an's army 
to the front-line camp.

15:30.017 --> 15:33.207
Chagatai is here now 
to see the Great Kha'an.

15:33.547 --> 15:37.707
Once we depart, we won't be seeing
 Chagatai for a long time.

15:37.927 --> 15:40.107
<i>In order to cause turmoil
 among the Mongols,</i>

15:40.107 --> 15:42.997
<i>we need a faction that will oppose 
the House of Tolui.</i>

15:42.997 --> 15:45.287
<i>The House of Chagatai 
is an indispensable part of that.</i>

15:45.937 --> 15:51.727
Then, allow me to go as your messenger
 and greet Prince Chagatai.

15:52.137 --> 15:54.437
I, Fatima, am your humble servant.

16:20.177 --> 16:22.637
Sir Qadaq, why are you following me?

16:22.637 --> 16:24.547
I can't let you go by yourself.

16:24.547 --> 16:26.947
Oh, I never took you 
to be such a gentleman.

16:26.947 --> 16:29.217
No, I'm saying I don't trust you.

16:29.217 --> 16:31.927
Lady Töregene has trust in me.

16:32.337 --> 16:34.417
She's not the one I serve.

16:34.807 --> 16:38.897
Long story, but right now, 
I'm acting on someone else's orders.

16:52.497 --> 16:55.077
Huh? Aren't you Töregene's slave?

16:55.397 --> 16:58.167
What are you doing out here?

16:58.787 --> 16:59.957
<i>Th-This woman is...</i>

17:00.437 --> 17:03.017
<i>Lady Möge, the fourth wife 
of the Great Kha'an!</i>

17:03.017 --> 17:06.717
Oh, I see. You don't learn, do you?

17:07.177 --> 17:09.487
<i>Wh-What? What?</i>

17:11.237 --> 17:12.467
You must be lost.

17:13.317 --> 17:15.307
Well? You are, aren't you?

17:15.307 --> 17:19.437
I bet you still haven't learned 
the locations of all the tents.

17:19.767 --> 17:23.277
I had my suspicions ever since 
you got caught wandering around last time.

17:23.277 --> 17:26.067
Töregene's explanation 
didn't seem truthful, either.

17:26.277 --> 17:27.197
Or perhaps—

17:27.197 --> 17:30.157
Y-You've found me out!

17:30.157 --> 17:31.287
I figured as much.

17:31.287 --> 17:35.917
What do I do? I'll bring shame upon 
Lady Töregene and be scolded again!

17:36.337 --> 17:39.137
It's none of my business 
if Töregene scolds you,

17:39.137 --> 17:41.827
but bringing shame upon the Great Kha'an
 is another matter.

17:41.827 --> 17:43.127
Allow me to show the way.

17:43.857 --> 17:46.847
I cannot thank you enough, Lady Möge!

17:47.427 --> 17:49.387
<i>I need to find my way out of this somehow.</i>

17:50.567 --> 17:53.597
<i>Something about Lady Möge 
seems different than last time.</i>

17:54.997 --> 17:56.237
Her earrings.

17:58.847 --> 18:00.067
I'm so sorry!

18:01.307 --> 18:03.937
Do I look strange without them?

18:04.387 --> 18:09.067
N-No, I wouldn't say "strange"
 as such, but...

18:10.707 --> 18:13.697
Did you happen to lose them?

18:15.397 --> 18:16.117
No.

18:16.747 --> 18:19.037
The Great Kha'an sold them.

18:19.037 --> 18:21.457
Great Kha'an! O Great Kha'an!

18:21.457 --> 18:24.047
I beseech you to buy this melon from me.

18:24.047 --> 18:26.297
I am ever so impoverished.

18:26.297 --> 18:27.967
What a small melon.

18:27.967 --> 18:31.067
Möge, give this man your earrings.

18:31.067 --> 18:31.967
What?

18:38.127 --> 18:39.437
Don't be distraught, Möge.

18:40.527 --> 18:45.567
I believe those earrings 
will return to you in the future.

18:46.027 --> 18:49.087
Return to you? What could he have meant?

18:49.087 --> 18:53.317
I haven't a clue. I don't understand 
the Great Kha'an in the slightest.

18:53.317 --> 18:54.417
Lady Möge!

18:55.347 --> 18:57.827
Lady Möge, the Great Kha'an
 is asking for you.

18:58.187 --> 18:59.377
What does he want?

18:59.377 --> 19:01.287
I wasn't informed of the details.

19:02.477 --> 19:03.137
Chuu!

19:05.437 --> 19:06.747
It won't be long now.

19:09.777 --> 19:10.967
Oh, there she is.

19:10.967 --> 19:12.587
Greetings, Möge.

19:13.097 --> 19:14.227
Come sit by me.

19:20.307 --> 19:21.727
I have here a gift for you.

19:26.017 --> 19:26.947
It can't be...

19:33.517 --> 19:35.147
My earrings!

19:35.457 --> 19:37.327
Where did you obtain these?

19:37.597 --> 19:40.117
That would be Khorasan.

19:40.117 --> 19:42.687
While on my journey to Samarkand,

19:42.687 --> 19:47.997
I was fortunate enough to meet a man 
selling fine treasures from the east.

19:52.267 --> 19:56.557
I asked him where he came across
 such splendid pearls.

19:56.557 --> 20:00.387
He told me he found them 
by a stroke of luck in a Uyghur city.

20:00.387 --> 20:05.807
He traded them for bread from a poor man 
on the verge of starving to death.

20:08.417 --> 20:12.027
Khorasan, is it? They traveled 
farther than I thought.

20:12.027 --> 20:16.847
Earrings so splendid as these 
befit the conqueror of the world.

20:16.847 --> 20:21.157
That is why I came here to present them 
as an offering, Great Kha'an.

20:23.387 --> 20:26.377
<i>They really returned to me.</i>

20:27.297 --> 20:29.357
Thank you for delivering them.

20:29.357 --> 20:32.807
I will buy all of your goods and 
those of the merchants accompanying you.

20:33.297 --> 20:34.977
Thank you very much.

20:34.977 --> 20:36.137
<i>All</i> of them?

20:36.467 --> 20:40.237
Bring me more wares in the future.
 You won't regret it.

20:47.327 --> 20:49.727
Um, over there, if you would.

20:49.727 --> 20:51.287
Put them with all the others.

20:51.287 --> 20:52.567
Be careful handling that.

20:53.317 --> 20:55.777
I didn't think he'd buy everything.

20:56.057 --> 20:58.367
Coming to Mongolia was the right decision.

20:58.637 --> 20:59.637
Excuse me.

21:01.367 --> 21:04.657
Have you traveled here from Khorasan?

21:04.657 --> 21:06.417
We did. Who are you?

21:06.417 --> 21:09.097
I hail from Khorasan as well.

21:09.097 --> 21:11.747
Why have you made your way to Mongolia?

21:11.747 --> 21:13.167
Why, you ask?

21:13.687 --> 21:18.317
Because Mongolia is where the most profit 
is to be had, of course.

21:18.317 --> 21:25.347
The Mongol emperor was likely to pay the 
most for wares from Khorasan and the west.

21:25.567 --> 21:27.937
Weren't you afraid to come here?

21:28.247 --> 21:32.177
The journey is a long one, 
and the Mongols are a frightening people.

21:32.547 --> 21:35.897
Not at all. In fact, it's safer 
to travel now than before.

21:37.157 --> 21:40.537
The Mongols appoint officials 
to govern the lands they conquer.

21:40.537 --> 21:43.287
Their duty is to protect merchants
 passing through.

21:43.917 --> 21:46.957
The emperor is a remarkable man, indeed.

21:47.277 --> 21:52.067
Thanks to your earrings, I've ascertained
that all is functioning as it should.

21:58.847 --> 22:05.537
Will everyone see things my way 
after we defeat the Jin?

22:14.487 --> 22:18.327
